<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 315)</h2>
<p><b>Web seats can now join Record the Session.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>When you record the session, browser participants get an invitation with plain-language consent: their microphone audio is end-to-end encrypted and uploaded for your Mac to transcribe (unlike desktop seats, whose audio never leaves their machine). Declining costs nothing but their voice in the minutes.</li>
<li>A consented web seat records one continuous take, visibly — a red chip stays on screen the whole time, and clicking it leaves the recording early (what was said still makes the minutes).</li>
<li>Their words land in the session minutes attributed by name, time-aligned to your recording and cross-talk-deduped, exactly like desktop participants.</li>
<li>Web recording audio uploads as sealed 2&nbsp;MB chunks; the host stitches them back into one take before transcribing, so nothing is lost at chunk boundaries. End Review wipes the audio with everything else.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
